            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0334" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/22</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-30T15:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1:01 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Mobilization decree issued. Most embassies and legations are informing their
                    governments that they consider war inevitable and I hold same opinion. German
                    and Austrian Embassies are packed and ready to leave any moment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
